{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a filesystem-enforced 100 MiB hard storage quota for `datauser`, whose home is `/srv/data`. The quota persisted across node1’s required reboot and remained directly enforceable.","actions_performed":["Installed Alpine quota tooling.","Created `datauser` and `/srv/data`.","Enabled persistent ext4 user quotas.","Set a 100 MiB hard block limit for `datauser`.","Verified enforcement before and after reboot with over-limit writes; both failed with `Quota exceeded`.","Removed test payloads while retaining `/srv/data/restart-proof.txt`.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified its boot identity changed."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"100 MiB filesystem quota under /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-7031d2a6ddfd4130","cmd-153828ed38c84769"],"summary":"Shows `datauser`, `/srv/data`, the 100M hard limit, and direct rejection of an over-limit write."},{"requirement":"Persistent quota configuration","command_ids":["cmd-a1835547c0c343c4","cmd-7d5494cb5fb041b6"],"summary":"Shows ext4 mounted with `usrquota`, persistent fstab configuration, and quota activation in Alpine’s default boot runlevel."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-0e717fb89e964ba0","cmd-ae7a6878e59e466d","cmd-44368224a27d4074","cmd-5e2f175451c44e7d","cmd-2c269d37b88a4ba1"],"summary":"Captures healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered quota/data state, and successful post-restart enforcement with final cleanup."}]}
